38
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:32,200
The Council has one special recognition. 6A is a resolution recognizing the accomplishments of the University of Alabama in Huntsville's UAH eSports program.

39
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,200
The Chair moves for approval.

40
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,200
Second.

41
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:37,200
Second from Mr. Kling. All in favor, please indicate.

42
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,200
Aye.

43
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,200
Opposed? The motion carries.

44
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:44,200
I have the pleasure of presenting this resolution.

45
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,200
Yep.

46
00:04:45,200 --> 00:05:02,200
Sports members, if you will please come.

47
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:08,200
This is a big team because it actually represents four teams, right?

48
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:12,200
So, I'll be down here with you.

49
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:19,200
Let me just share with you this resolution because some of you may not even know what eSports are.

50
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:35,200
Whereas the City Council and the Mayor of the City of Huntsville, Alabama, wish to recognize the outstanding accomplishments of the University of Alabama in Huntsville UAH eSports and its student athletes for their exceptional performances during the 2025-2026 competitive eSports season.

51
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:53,200
And whereas UAH eSports competed in the National eSports Collegiate Conference, NECC, one of the nation's premier collegiate eSports organizations and demonstrated remarkable success this season with nine of its 27 teams qualifying for the national tournament.

52
00:05:53,200 --> 00:06:05,200
And whereas four UAH eSports teams advanced to the deepest stages of their respective national playoff brackets, showcasing the program's talent, dedication, and teamwork on a national stage.

53
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:24,200
And whereas UAH's Valorant Blue Team captured the NECC National Championship on May 4th following an already impressive season in which the team also secured a regional championship victory, further establishing itself among the nation's collegiate eSports teams.

54
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:42,200
And whereas UAH's Marvel Rivals Blue Team earned a place among the top competitors nationally, advancing to compete against California State University Sacramento for third place in the national tournament bracket after finishing fourth in the regional playoff competition.

55
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:55,200
Whereas UAH's Counter-Strike White Team advanced to compete for an NECC National Championship title after also earning a regional championship victory earlier in the year.

56
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,200
There's more.

57
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:13,200
Whereas UAH's League of Legends Blue Team also won a regional championship title in the 2025 season. And whereas within the UAH eSports program, Blue Teams represent varsity level competition and White Teams represent junior varsity level competition.

58
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:22,200
And the success achieved by both levels of teams reflects the continued growth and national prominence of eSports at the University of Alabama in Huntsville.

59
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:45,200
Now therefore, be it resolved that the City Council and the Mayor of the City of Huntsville, Alabama do hereby recognize and commend the accomplishments of UAH eSports and its student competitors and extend immense appreciation to the pride and distinction these teams have brought to the University and the Huntsville community during their commitment, sportsmanship and competitive excellence.

60
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:49,200
Join me in congratulating our UAH eSports teams.

61
00:07:49,200 --> 00:08:00,200
And now let me turn this over to Efren Hummel who will tell us a little bit more about what this really represents.

62
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:09,200
Absolutely. Thank you so much for the beautiful words. We are very honored to be here in front of you all today and in front of all of the viewers watching as well.

63
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:17,200
UAH eSports or the eSports club at UAH is an absolute staple of the UAH campus. We're very glad to be able to do what we do.

64
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:26,200
Currently we have about 130 competitive members across our 27 teams. So it is one of the largest clubs on campus and we're very proud of that.

65
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:38,200
And we're very proud of these teams as well for excelling in their playoff divisions and committing the time as well required in order to practice and scrimmage and stay at the highest levels of competition.

66
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:48,200
These athletes that stand before you are the best of the best and we're very happy to be here. Down the line I will introduce a few of our different teams.

67
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:57,200
So Prem right here is one of the representatives from our League of Legends team. These two right here are new officers for the eSports program.

68
00:08:57,200 --> 00:09:06,200
Here in the middle is our two representatives from Valorant. Marvel Rivals standing here third to the right and finally Counter-Strike at the very end.

69
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:14,200
I got the pleasure of coaching our Counter-Strike team as well. And I forgot to introduce myself. I'm sorry. My name is Ethan Hummel. I am the student director of eSports at UAH.

70
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:25,200
And so I've been very pleased to have this position to be able to lead at an advisory level for the club and direct what the new officers are able to do.

71
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:27,200
So thank you so much for this opportunity.

72
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:37,200
Well thank you for your service to these team members and I will also point out that my grandson Alex Austin was on the national championship Blue Valorant team.

73
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:58,200
So that's a special thing for us. So again join me in congratulating our eSports team.

74
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,200
Thank you.

75
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:39,200
Thank you.

76
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:29,200
We do a lot of important things at these meetings but I think nothing is as important as recognizing the good work that's being done by a lot of different people in our community.

77
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:48,200
We have no announcements and presentations. No matters with legal representatives and this brings us to public hearings to be held.

78
00:11:48,200 --> 00:12:03,200
9A is a public hearing on a resolution authorizing the demolition of an unsafe building constituting a public nuisance located at 3804 Melody Road, Northeast Huntsville, Alabama and consideration of a resolution pertaining to the same. Mr. Irwin.

79
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:25,200
Yes, Councilmembers, Mayor Battle, Scott Irwin, Community Development Department. This is an appeal of community development findings related to the property on Melody Drive. The resolution, pardon me, the appeal of the community development findings and a public hearing on a resolution authorizing the demolition of the unsafe building constituting a public nuisance at 3804 Melody Drive.

80
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:37,200
The owners and entry parties were notified of the public hearing by certified mail and first class mail. The entry parties indicated they intended to appear before you to present any objections. We have photographs of the property for your review on the screen.

81
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:46,200
The property was initially inspected by an independent contractor who determined the structure was not structurally feasible for repair. It totaled out a 98 percent loss.

82
00:12:46,200 --> 00:13:01,200
An official notice was sent by certified and first class mail requesting demolition and removal of the structure by April 22, 2026. No action was taken by the owners or entry parties, so we are here before you tonight requesting authorization to abate this public nuisance.

83
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:14,200
Thank you, Mr. Irwin. The public hearing is now open. I believe the property owners are here if you would like to approach the podium here. And if you will give us your name and address for the record, please.

84
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:21,200
Thank you so much. My name is LaRoy Barley, 9717 Rock Creek Road, Raleigh, North Carolina.

85
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:23,200
Thank you. Please proceed.

86
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:47,200
How are you doing? We are here, as Yafra mentioned, to really ask for consideration of more time in assessing the situation with this property. We have contacted and talked to several contractors who have looked at it externally, and because of the notice on it, et cetera, no one has gone in it to check.

87
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:55,200
We're one of the things we'd like to ask is to be able to proceed to go inside. We have stayed away from doing that because of the notice to not want to go in.

88
00:13:55,200 --> 00:14:14,200
Other thing is travel. My sister and I think was mentioned that we live out of state quite a distance away. And just getting here can be difficult. We do have family who has kept a watch on it and things of that nature, make sure the property is stayed closed, which it has, et cetera.

89
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:28,200
So that is kind of where we are with that. One of the things that has, as the people we have discussed this with as far as contractors, no one has given us or counseled us in that it needs to be torn down.

90
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:40,200
Everyone has been very encouraging, saying, no, this can be saved. But they have wanted to go inside, and we just have not gone in because we didn't think we were permitted to at this time with the notice and what have you.

91
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:55,200
Myself and my older brother, we have gone in it in times prior to the notice being said that you could not. And it does look like, you know, being around these things before a property that could be saved, even though there is, we know it's great work that is needed and there will be a cost.

92
00:14:55,200 --> 00:15:13,200
Post that or past that, once we determine what that cost would be, how extensive, we would like then to make a decision on how we proceed from there. We just don't think it is necessary to tear it down without an adequate assessment of what would be needed and get full numbers on that.

93
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:24,200
We just have not been able to conclude that currently because we have not been able to get inside the property. We have only been able to assess it from the outside with those that have been able to look at it this far.

94
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:29,200
Thank you, Mr. Barley. Is there anyone else who wishes to comment?

95
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:33,200
Anyone else wishing to comment? Then the public hearing is closed.

96
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:37,200
Is there a motion to approve the resolution?

97
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:40,200
Motion from Mr. Little, second from the chair.

98
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:42,200
Now discussion.

99
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:44,200
Yes.

100
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:46,200
Mr. Erwin.

101
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:50,200
Do you know if the house is safe for anyone to go inside and inspect it?

102
00:15:50,200 --> 00:16:01,200
So when a property has been deemed unsafe, so you are not allowed to enter that property because it would be a danger of liability. So at this point, no, based on that fact, it is not suitable for someone to enter.

103
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:03,200
So it is not structurally sound?

104
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,200
Correct.

105
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:07,200
Okay. Has anyone from the family been in contact with you?

106
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:21,200
Yes, I spoke with the family back in April and explained the process that we would do to move forward on our position, which the property was beyond a renovation or rehabilitation type activity.

107
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:33,200
And based on the independent contractor assessment, which was a 98 percent loss, as staff, we deemed that it was appropriate for this property to be demolished.

108
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:43,200
So even with the notice not to enter, they couldn't enter with a different contractor and one of the community development member?

109
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:57,200
So yes, the contractor could, but not for individuals could not. It would have to be someone who has license able to evaluate whatever the necessary structural integrity aspects are being evaluated are.

110
00:16:57,200 --> 00:17:10,200
Okay. So in the intervening time between when it's supposed to be demolished and today, if they could get a contractor in there before it's torn down and they decide that it is salvageable, what would happen?

111
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:21,200
Yeah, our position as staff that it still is beyond that. However, we could arrange for them to review that. We are still going forward and asking your authorization to abate the nuisance.

112
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:22,200
Okay. Thank you.

113
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,200
And what's your timeline on that?

114
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:32,200
So we normally take the minimum of 30 days being under public works schedule going forward. It is a busy time. It could go slightly more than that.

115
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:39,200
But everyone typically does have a minimum of 30 days before we are actually able to mobilize and move forward with any demolition.

116
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,200
Mr. Kling.

117
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:49,200
Question or just an idea to throw out on the table since the only time we really get to talk about these things is in this venue.

118
00:17:49,200 --> 00:18:02,200
What if we were to give approval for Mr. Irwin to proceed as he sees fit, including demolition, time extension or whatever?

119
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:13,200
What we've done in the past, we basically give him the hammer and we trust his judgment if it looks like there's some light at the end of the tunnel.

120
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:23,200
But at the same time to counter that, to throw out, how would the people who live in that neighborhood feel about what I think is a pretty bad blight?

121
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:30,200
Do they want to have this extend longer or have we been hearing any complaints from people in that neighborhood?

122
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:34,200
So that's a double edged sword I'm throwing out.

123
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,200
So your proposal is to move forward with.

124
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:45,200
No, well actually I'm just kind of throwing out on the table both arguments to see if there's some consensus on the council as far as what to do.

125
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:48,200
Mr. Meredith, I believe you have a comment.

126
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:55,200
If the only way to do that is for you to put up a motion for an amendment and us to vote on that.

127
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:58,200
Well, that's what I was trying to ascertain.

128
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:02,200
So we have a motion right now on the floor to proceed with demolition.

129
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:16,200
As I understand that will not take place for 30 days and in that 30 days time period, if the Barlow family had a contractor, you would permit that contractor to go into the building to make an evaluation?

130
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,200
That's correct.

131
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:19,200
We would handle this as we do all of our public nuisance activities.

132
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:27,200
We would work with the owner for the most equitable way to get this property secured and removed if needed.

133
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:37,200
If there's an argument to be made by an independent contractor that it is ready and able to be renovated with a budget and a timeline, then we would certainly be willing to look at that.

134
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:39,200
Any other questions or comments?

135
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:44,200
So they have 30 days before it's going to be demolition, scheduled to be demolition.

136
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:59,200
So during that time frame, hopefully Mr. Barley can get with you and schedule a time for a contractor to come out and then that way we would know even if we vote if there's a possibility for the House to be redeemed.

137
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:00,200
Absolutely.

138
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,200
Absolutely.

139
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,200
Okay.

140
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:03,200
Okay.

141
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,200
Any other comments?

142
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:06,200
All in favor, please indicate.

143
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,200
Aye.

144
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:08,200
Any opposed?

145
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:10,200
The motion carries.

146
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:11,200
Thank you, Councilman.

147
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:17,200
Mr. Barley, we will let you meet with Mr. Irwin to work out how you can get that contractor to take a look.

148
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:19,200
Thank you for being with us tonight.

149
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:21,200
Safe travels back to Raleigh.

