01:10:04,200 --> 01:10:12,200
Lots of other supporters, if y'all would like to stand up just to show them who's here would be great.

607
01:10:12,200 --> 01:10:19,200
The two lives that day was a 36 year old father and eight year old little girl gone in a moment that should have never been left so unprotected.

608
01:10:19,200 --> 01:10:24,200
Two families changed forever at a crossing that gave no warning, no barrier, no second chance.

609
01:10:24,200 --> 01:10:30,200
These are not isolated stories. They're reminders. A train can't swerve, it can't stop quickly.

610
01:10:30,200 --> 01:10:42,200
And when a crossing has no lights, no gates, no protective barriers at all, the responsibility falls entirely on human judgment and the conditions are often hard to judge.

611
01:10:42,200 --> 01:10:53,200
This is why safety upgrades matter. Lights, bells, crossing arms are not luxuries. They're life saving barriers between everyday travel and irreversible loss.

612
01:10:53,200 --> 01:11:07,200
Every crossing like Salty Bottom Road, a crossing that has more than 2,100 vehicles that cross it every single day, a crossing that's had multiple fatalities, a crossing that remains unprotected is a risk sitting in plain sight.

613
01:11:07,200 --> 01:11:16,200
City Council members, I respectfully ask for your help along with all of these people and several that couldn't come because they couldn't get off work.

614
01:11:16,200 --> 01:11:26,200
In addressing the ongoing safety concerns at this railroad crossing at Salty Bottom, please work with ALDOT to make the necessary improvements before another tragedy occurs.

